step("p7-tree36",S[6],"Let us break 36 in four different ways. First two times eighteen, then eighteen is two times nine, and nine is three times three. Second, three times twelve, then twelve is three times four, and four is two times two. Third, four times nine. Fourth, six times six, and each six is two times three. Look at the last row of every tree: each has two 2s and two 3s. Different paths, the same primes.","36 ஐ நான்கு வழிகளில் பிரிப்போம். முதலில் 2×18; 18 = 2×9; 9 = 3×3. இரண்டாவது 3×12; 12 = 3×4; 4 = 2×2. மூன்றாவது 4×9. நான்காவது 6×6; ஒவ்வொரு 6 உம் 2×3. ஒவ்வொரு மரத்தின் கடைசி வரிசையிலும் இரண்டு 2 உம் இரண்டு 3 உம் உள்ளன. வழிகள் வேறு; பகா எண்கள் ஒன்றே.",[CL]+wr(["t36h"],0.02,0,500)+[x for ti in range(4) for x in sh(["t36n%dr%d"%(ti,ri) for ri in range(4)],0.1+ti*0.2,0.045,350)]+wr(["t36f"],0.95,0,500))
